{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/352859-no-humanity-variant","id":352859,"title":"No Humanity Variant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-28T10:54:36-08:00","id":352859,"title":"No Humanity Variant?","content":"When we updated from 1st edition Requiem to 2nd edition, Humanity was much improved as a concept and a mechanic; however, I find it still just doesn't work well for me and some of my group. I'd therefore like to try out a rules variant where there just isn't a humanity stat at all, and see how it goes. Of course, in 2E humanity is interwoven into many mechanics, so it's a bit more involved than just removing it. Here are my current thoughts on mechanics that would need some adjusting:<br /> <br /> <b>The Basics:</b> Blood Potency would probably take a lot of the functions of Humanity onto itself. Each age category of vampire has an average humanity (the book speaks of things like &quot;most ancillae fall in this category&quot; and stuff), so tying some of this stuff to the other stat that's influenced most by age seems to make sense. Humanity was also one of the big limits on the Embrace and diablerie, and I can see plausible ways to tie this into BP instead. (Diablerie does it on its own, and a connection between the Embrace and how fast your blood thickens doesn't seem too far-fetched.)<br /> <br /> I'm considering using Blood Beats in some form to supplement BP growth, sort of making those who act more vampiric thicken faster, and thus getting to the problem points faster. Like how those who act more vampiric drop humanity faster, too. Way too fast if you ask me, if I played my players through 50 years of night to night play, they'd never manage to still be at the &quot;ancillae&quot; level of humanity. I'm toying with the idea to make BP cost 5xp times your current BP rank to go up to the next level, so that it doesn't shoot up too fast.<br /> <br /> <b>Social Penalties:</b> Truth be told, these flat social penalties low humanity gives you is one of the things I and some of my players just don't like too much. If I do want to keep them though, it's simple to tie that to BP. You just invert the table: penalties rise as BP gets higher, rather than rising as humanity gets higher.<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstones:</b> I like touchstones. In fact, I love them. I don't want to throw the child out with the bath water and get rid of them too, but their main purpose is somewhat diluted without the humanity mechanic. A bonus to resisting frenzy for having touchstones, perhaps? Their willpower regaining properties are still useful of course, and maybe just making it a bit easier to get wp back from them (it's quite hard to get wp back in our group, so there's room for improvement there) might keep them useful. I truly detest the way dropping Humanity has my touchstones automatically detach, especially since I've frequently had a bout of bad luck turn two necessary evils into a quick 1-2-punch detachment of an interesting Touchstone (yeah, they're still there, but it's not the same), and then you have to face the xp tax... Over half the people in another game I'm in just don't have touchstones anymore as they dropped so fast in a short period of time that the xp tax it'd take to reach their level doesn't seem worth it to them, with the risk that they detach right away.<br /> <br /> Players will have to work to keep their relationships to their touchstones up, and they can detach if they mess up or estrange them somehow. I've always preferred running things like this purely through cause and effect rather than a tangentially related failed dice roll. I suppose that it would be possible to attach them again too, maybe with Social Maneuvering and some effort. Might be a good place to put the Ventrue curse in place, or penalties form high BP.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Banes:</b> The gap between BP1 and 2 is higher than Humanity 7 and 6, so I'm thinking of having it in effect right away. At most maybe a delayed onset of 1d10 weeks could be considered. Mekhet would count as higher BP for banes rather than lower humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Sunlight:</b> Either make both interval and damage based upon BP, fix one of the two at a steady rate, or have one of them decided by something else. I'm thinking of just doing something like this base don BP:<br /> 0: No sunlight damage.<br /> 1: 1 lethal/10 minutes<br /> 2: 2 lethal/10 minutes<br /> 3: 2 lethal/1 minute<br /> 4: 2 lethal/turn<br /> 5: 1 aggravated/turn<br /> 6: 1 aggravated/twice per turn<br /> 7: 2 aggravated/twice per turn<br /> 8: 2 aggravated/thrice per turn<br /> 9: 3 aggravated/thrice per turn<br /> 10: 4 aggravated, 4 times in a turn.<br /> <br /> A different progression than normal, but it works. In general this means vampires can be &quot;ok&quot; at being in sunlight for a bit longer than in your average game, but I'm fine with that.<br /> <br /> <b>Banes:</b> I'm thinking of redesigning these a bit, making both &quot;lesser&quot; and &quot;greater&quot; banes. You would then automatically acquire banes at certain BP levels, like a minor at BP2 to start, and go from there. Minor banes would probably give penalties to certain actions after encountering or sinning against the bane (the size of the penalty equal to BP, probably), while greater ones likely do damage or have other equally bad effects. I'd like to get some simple guidelines together so GM and players can make up a bane for a character easily and have it fit them, the current list is a bit hit or miss.<br /> <br /> <b>Daysleep:</b> Replace humanity with Sta + Resolve, with a bonus for low BP (small) and then -1 from that for every BP you go up. Considering not giving the bonus from Resilience to this, similar to how Vigor doesn't give a bonus to Lashing Out with the Monstrous Beast. Speaking of those...<br /> <br /> <b>The 3 Conditions of the Beast:</b> Bestial, Competitive and Wanton have some resolutions dealing with Humanity. I never liked those anyway, so those were already house ruled to not use humanity resolutions. &quot;Indulge a vice at a personal risk, or...&quot; and stuff like that. Not too hard.<br /> <br /> <b>Torpor: </b>Just base it off BP. I've never been in a game where the exact length of a lengthy torpor was important anyway. Perhaps make torpor degrade BP a bit faster, making a dynamic where vampires both go up faster in BP and go down faster. Maybe.<br /> <br /> <b>Diablerie:</b> I believe more in social repercussions to keep people in check, so I'm not worried about losing breaking points for this. It makes BP go up, which will also give more banes, make them affect you more, and the like. That seems sufficient to me next to the social stigma and risk of discovery.<br /> <br /> <b>Embrace (and Ghouling, to some extent):</b> Same as Diablerie, I believe more in social repercussions. Go ahead and Embrace away, but be prepared for your sudden flock of neonates to set half the city on fire, piss off every other Vampire and bring several Hunter conspiracies knocking on your door. I'm toying with the idea of making the Embrace cost 1 or more Blood Beat XP; it sounds plausible that Embracing another makes your blood thin slower. I'm not sure if this wouldn't just be seen as a slow-bp-gain-down exploit though (but obviously, high BP makes you quite powerful, so maybe not.) Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, aside from some smaller things like changing some merits or specific powers, I think that's about it. Anyone notice something big missing? Got ideas on touchstones or other elements, done something like this yourself before, etc... ? Let me know!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-29-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T20:03:54-08:00","id":389337,"title":"","content":"So I know you posted this over a year ago but I'd like to know how it turned out. I'm starting a new game soon with my friends and we're going to switch over to the 2nd Edition. I've never been particularly fond of Humanity and though I agree that 2E Humanity is a step in the right direction I'd still like to run the game without it.<br /> So how did these houserules work out for you? Were you satisfied with the outcome? Did you make any tweaks that aren't covered above?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I misread the date you posted this. Thought it said 2013 instead of 2014. But that's awesome. That means this thread is still active as I can see now from the new posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","user":"baboonking","date":". 02-03-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:34:12-08:00","id":389888,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a variant can be devised where Touchstones represent Humanity in its totality. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I truly detest the way dropping Humanity has my touchstones automatically detach, especially since I've frequently had a bout of bad luck turn two necessary evils into a quick 1-2-punch detachment of an interesting Touchstone </div> </div> </div>Get rid of a drop in Humanity 'detaching' a Touchstone. Make humanity completely based on how connected you are to the human world. Nothing to do with morality or acting human, although those things may be important in order to stay connected to Touchstones themselves.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can devise rules where certain levels of Humanity represent specific requirements for Touchstones:<br /> <br /> HUMANITY<br /> 1 = no Touchstones<br /> 2 = at least one object as a Touchstone<br /> 3 = at least one place as a Touchstone<br /> 4 = at least one place and one object as Touchstones<br /> 5 = at least one person as a Touchstone<br /> 6 = at least one person and one object as Touchstones<br /> 7 = at least one person and one place as Touchstones<br /> 8 = at least one person, one place, and one object as Touchstones<br /> 9 = at least three persons as Touchstones<br /> 10 = at least four persons as Touchstones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 02-02-2015, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:41:59-08:00","id":389893,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that detached Touchstone is not forgotten completely. They still protect your humanity (tho in weaker ways) and allow you to regain WP. so if you have an interesting Touchstone - keep interacting with him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You still get your WP juice flowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T09:38:48-08:00","id":389949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/352859-no-humanity-variant?p=389893#post389893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that detached Touchstone is not forgotten completely. They still protect your humanity (tho in weaker ways) and allow you to regain WP. so if you have an interesting Touchstone - keep interacting with him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You still get your WP juice flowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now that Willpower is no longer recovered by rest interacting with Touchstones is probably the most steady method of recovery of such an important trait. [Shameless plug] That' why I based my homebrewed Ventrue Bane around that [/shameless plug] <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T09:59:37-08:00","id":389989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/352859-no-humanity-variant?p=389888#post389888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get rid of a drop in Humanity 'detaching' a Touchstone. Make humanity completely based on how connected you are to the human world. Nothing to do with morality or acting human, although those things may be important in order to stay connected to Touchstones themselves.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can devise rules where certain levels of Humanity represent specific requirements for Touchstones:<br /> <br /> HUMANITY<br /> 1 = no Touchstones<br /> 2 = at least one object as a Touchstone<br /> 3 = at least one place as a Touchstone<br /> 4 = at least one place and one object as Touchstones<br /> 5 = at least one person as a Touchstone<br /> 6 = at least one person and one object as Touchstones<br /> 7 = at least one person and one place as Touchstones<br /> 8 = at least one person, one place, and one object as Touchstones<br /> 9 = at least three persons as Touchstones<br /> 10 = at least four persons as Touchstones</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that as a concept, but I think there can be a little improvement. For example, a starting vampire, with Humanity 7, has a Touchstone of one person and one place. Let's say they have their favorite diner they like to frequent, and the Waitress who works there. If they lose the Diner, they drop to 5 Humanity, a bit harsh, but not too bad. If they lose the Waitress, they plummet all the way to 3. That seems a bit extreme to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:14:42-08:00","id":391653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/352859-no-humanity-variant?p=389949#post389949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now that Willpower is no longer recovered by rest interacting with Touchstones is probably the most steady method of recovery of such an important trait. [Shameless plug] That' why I based my homebrewed Ventrue Bane around that [/shameless plug] <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to join in on this shameless plug but could you post link to this homebrewed Ventrue Bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:31:59-08:00","id":391668,"title":"","content":"I think if I was going to drop Humanity, I'd treat most mechanics as if all characters had a 4, rather than trying to key them off different traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T13:26:21-08:00","id":391790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/352859-no-humanity-variant?p=391668#post391668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if I was going to drop Humanity, I'd treat most mechanics as if all characters had a 4, rather than trying to key them off different traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the curiosity in me... Why a 4? I am interested in your reasons behind that number. Why not a 3, or a 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:49:30-08:00","id":391964,"title":"","content":"The original post appears to be a riff off of one of the options found in <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b>. For reference purposes, <b>Mirrors</b> proposed the following changes:<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Base Time spent in Torpor:</b> use Stamina + Resolve instead of Humanity<br /> <b>\u2022 Remaining awake during the day:</b> use Stamina + Resolve - Blood Potency instead of Humanity<br /> <b>\u2022 Interacting with mortals:</b> use Blood Potency as a penalty to suitable rolls<br /> <br /> Of course, <b>Mirrors</b> was dealing with <b>VtR 1e</b>; and in <b>2e</b>, Humanity gets used for more/different things; so Unahim\u2019s proposals need to address those changes as well. Which, apparently, it does. <br /> <br /> There are also the \u201cAtrocities\u201d and \u201cHell Is Other People\u201d options mentioned in <b>Danse Macabre</b>, the latter being a spiritual predecessor of sorts of 2e\u2019s Touchstones. That said, neither really addresses what to do with cases where your Humanity score is referenced directly by the rules (such as being the basis for a dice pool, or being a resource you must expend); rather, they act as replacements for the detachment rolls: instead of having to roll against Humanity and risk lowering its score when you do something monstrous, the Atrocities rules give you \u201cAtrocity Dice\u201d for such actions that tend to poison appropriate rolls until you rid yourself of them; and instead of losing Touchstones whenever your Humanity drops below a certain threshold, \u201cHell Is Other People\u201d has a tracking system where your relationship with your \u201canchors\u201d gets corrupted and twisted into something depraved by such actions. In this regard, they\u2019re worth looking at; however, the question of what to do without a Humanity trait is still something that needs to be looked at: with Atrocities and/or HIOP in play instead of Humanity, how do you determine how long you spend in torpor or how well you\u2019re able to stay awake during the day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:45:54-08:00","id":396863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/352859-no-humanity-variant?p=389989#post389989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that as a concept, but I think there can be a little improvement. For example, a starting vampire, with Humanity 7, has a Touchstone of one person and one place. Let's say they have their favorite diner they like to frequent, and the Waitress who works there. If they lose the Diner, they drop to 5 Humanity, a bit harsh, but not too bad. If they lose the Waitress, they plummet all the way to 3. That seems a bit extreme to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. A simpler alternative, partially inspired by Rose's contribution, is that you have Humanity set at a default of five, and increase its value by one for each Touchstone you 'buy' via the already-in-place merit.<br /> <br /> The problem with completely dropping Humanity is that it can make Touchstones seem pretty irrelevant IMO.<br /> <br /> The aim: remove the moral aspects of Humanity, keep Touchstones relevant to Humanity. Make Humanity about keeping Touchstones safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T07:39:46-07:00","id":1536356,"title":"","content":"I love this, it feels more classically gothic to me. I typically just toss humanity out as I am a fan of external over internal consequences. My beloved Carmilla and lord Ruthven had no internal consequences, and they were very compelling vampires and peak gothic fiction in my opinion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}